# Deploy: pushing to `main` does NOT publish the site

GitHub Pages serves **from the `gh-pages` branch**, not `main`.
Deploy is a manual mirror `main → gh-pages` (workflow `.github/workflows/control-tower-actions.yml`,
`workflow_dispatch` → action `deploy`, which does `git push origin HEAD:gh-pages --force`).

So a commit on `main` alone will 404 on the live site. To publish:

```bash
# 1) commit + push main as usual
git push origin main

# 2) DEPLOY — mirror main into gh-pages (fast-forward if gh-pages is an ancestor)
git fetch origin gh-pages main -q
git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/gh-pages origin/main && echo "ff-safe"
git push origin main:gh-pages   # matches the control-tower "deploy" action
```

## Verify it went live
- Pages CDN (Fastly) rebuilds ~1–2 min after `gh-pages` updates.
- Check freshness via `journal.html` `last-modified` header, not just the new URL.
- **Negative cache gotcha**: a URL hit while still 404 gets negative-cached on the
  CDN; use a cache-bust query (`?v=$(date +%s)`) to confirm the file is really live,
  then the plain URL clears shortly after.

## After deploy
- Ping IndexNow (Yandex/Bing) for changed URLs: `./indexnow.sh <url> ...`
  (or `./indexnow.sh --recent` for URLs in the last commit).
